docs/backlog.md:107:**D156 — DEVDESK-412 (security): the registry HTTP clients DEVDESK-410 left out get the same origin and size hardening, and a template blob may be served from another origin, without credentials. Decided (user, 2026-11-16, questions of the plan `.claude/plans/DEVDESK-412-plan.md`): (Q1b) the layer blob of an OCI template follows a redirect to another host, without `Authorization` or `Referer` and without any retry with credentials. *This is an explicit exception to the story's "out of scope: CDN redirect support"*; every other call (template tags and manifest, registry tags, catalog, token, Nexus) keeps refusing an off-origin redirect (D142). (Q2) `oci.Client` has a 1 minute timeout for a whole request, redirects and body included. (Q3) an `http://` Bearer realm behind an `https` registry is refused, with or without credentials (this closes D142's residual risk of the clear-text realm); a realm that is neither `http` nor `https` is refused too. (Q4) the registry URL is redacted in `browser_bridge.go` and in the error prefixes of `registry.go` (`RedactURL`; closes D142's raw-URL residual risk). (Q5a) the digest of the layer is always checked, redirected or not: `sha256:` and 64 lowercase hex digits only, so a registry whose layers are `sha512` is refused. (Q6) no redirect from `https` to `http` (compared with the previous hop); the SSRF guard is loopback and link-local only (`localhost`, `*.localhost`, `0.0.0.0` and literal addresses; private ranges are not filtered). What shipped: `internal/oci/guard.go` exports `MaxRedirects`, `ErrOffOriginRedirect`, `ErrTooManyRedirects`, `RefuseOffOriginRedirect`, `StripRedirectTarget`, `ErrBodyTooLarge`, `ReadAllLimited`, `RedactURL`, `RedactRegistryURL` (address with or without scheme, host kept readable; used by the `browser_bridge.go`, `registries.go` and `commands.go` logs; `redactGitURL` in `internal/template/fetch.go` masks a git source URL in `fetching ...` for `http(s)`, scp form unchanged, and also a