igured proxy for every connection of the transport, not only those `Proxy()` decided: with `NO_PROXY`, a name that resolves to that port stays reachable directly, as an anonymous `GET`; (5) when the registry is local (`localhost`, loopback, link-local) no SSRF filter applies; (6) an `http` registry can redirect the blob to any `http` URL, bounded by the loopback and link-local filter when the registry is not local; (7) CPU: a very compressible entry or PAX headers can make the tar reader decompress up to about 34 GiB, bounded by the 1 minute timeout, before the digest check, with no memory cost; (8) the unverified tar.gz is parsed in memory before the digest check, bounded by `Limits`; nothing is returned or cached before the check; (9) the digest is limited to sha256 (a sha512 layer is refused); (10) integrity is that of the manifest (a mutable tag), with no signature verification; (11) a Bearer `https` realm may be on another host and receives the Basic credentials (standard Docker behavior); (12) Nexus refuses `http` to `https` on the same host (the scheme is part of the origin), so enter the URL in `https`; its 1 MiB cap is not measured; the anonymous retry starts on any error except the origin refusal; (13) `oci.Client.ListTags` decodes an unbounded body (unused in production), and 410's own bounded reads were not moved onto `ReadAllLimited`; (14) each `NewClient` clones a `Transport` whose idle connections stay about 90 s (a resource, not a leak). No ADR: local and reversible by a revert. **Plane:** DEVDESK-412 (story), DEVDESK-523 (412-9, docs), dated 2026-11-16. Sources: `.claude/plans/DEVDESK-412-plan.md`, `docs/architecture/network.md`, `internal/oci/guard.go`, `internal/oci/oci_blob.go`; D142, D149.**
docs/backlog.md:135:**D142 — DEVDESK-410 (security): `internal/oci` no longer sends registry credentials or follows a link off the origin they were meant for, and bounds the token response. Three pre-existing weaknesses found by the security review of DEVDESK-306 (D135) are fixed: (1) the `Link: rel="next"` of the tag list is no longer followed off-origin (`sameOrigin`); a foreign `next` is an error wrapping the sentinel `ErrTagsNextOffOrigin` (`errors.Is`, destination host only), with no partial list, because a short list could give `imageupdate` and the security remediation a false "up to date" (the catalog walker keeps `truncated=true` with the names already read); (2) `registryHTTPClient` has a `CheckRedirect` (`refuseOffOriginRedirect`) that refuses any redirect leaving the origin of the first request (scheme, host and port, compared against `via[0]`), instead of following it without `Authorization`. The choice: an explicit error is safer than a silent anonymous retry; the error is `refusing redirect to another origin (host)`, wraps `errOffOriginRedirect`, and carries no target path or query (a signed URL reaches neither footer nor logs). Consequence: a registry that redirects to another host is unusable with this client, and some redirects once followed are now refused (http to https on the same host, `host` to `host:443`, a different host case: exact scheme and host:port, refused when in doubt); (3) the Bearer token endpoint's response is capped at 1 MiB (`maxTokenResponse`), and a larger body is an error, not a silent cut. Residual risks found and not fixed: a Bearer `realm` in `http://` announced by an https registry sends the Basic credentials in clear (initial request, outside this fix); and `registry.go` puts the raw request URL in the error prefix, so a userinfo in `apiURL` would appear there (pre-existing). Found and not fixed, out of scope: `internal/oci/oci.go:46` (`http.Client` with neither `CheckRedirect` nor timeout, registry credentials), `intern